{"name":"Carolina Parakeet","hex":"#d8df80","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"parakeet","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of various species of small parrot primarily of tropical regions. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/parakeet"}],"entries":[{"title":"Carolina parakeet","blocks":[{"text":"The Carolina parakeet, or Carolina conure, is an extinct species of small green neotropical parrot with a bright yellow head, reddish orange face, and pale beak that was native to the Eastern, Midwest, and Plains States of the United States. It was the only indigenous parrot within its range, and one of only three parrot species native to the United States. The others are the thick-billed parrot, now extirpated; and the green parakeet, still present in Texas. A fourth parrot species, the red-crowned amazon, is debated."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f6/Naturalis_Biodiversity_Center_-_ZMA.AVES.3159_-_Conuropsis_carolinensis_Linnaeus%2C_1758_-_Psittacidae_-_skin_specimen.jpeg/330px-Naturalis_Biodiversity_Center_-_ZMA.AVES.3159_-_Conuropsis_carolinensis_Linnaeus%2C_1758_-_Psittacidae_-_skin_specimen.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Carolina_parakeet","wikidata":"Q629204"},{"title":"Parakeet","blocks":[{"text":"A parakeet is any one of many small- to medium-sized species of parrot, in multiple genera, that generally has long tail feathers. Most species belong to the genus Pyrrhura."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a5/Male_and_female_parakeet_1.jpg/330px-Male_and_female_parakeet_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Parakeet","wikidata":"Q8329"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/30/Carolina_Parakeet_Range.jpg/500px-Carolina_Pa